# Actions
It is now possible to define "actions".
## Action: skipTime
For now, it is just a single action to skip a specified amount of time for a specific set of timers.
### Example:
```json
      "actions": [
        {
          "name": "Skip Time",
          "type": "skipTime",
          "sets": ["boss"],
          "time": 1.0,
          "trigger": { "position": [-0.242, -101.378], "radius": 60,
            "type": "key", "keyBind": "1",
            "requireEntry": true
          }
        }
      ]
```
```json
      "alerts": [
        {
          "warning": "Shadows soon...", "alert": "Shadows!", "fillColor": [0, 50, 255, 0],
          "warningDuration": 9.5, "alertDuration": 5, "timestamps": [39, 106, 173, 240, 307, 374],
          "set": "boss"
        }
      ]
```
### Structure:
```json
{
  // ...
  "phases": [
    {
      // ...
      "actions": [
        {
          "name": "Example Action",
          "type": "skipTime",         // If not specified, its auto predefined to "skipTime" for now
          "sets": ["set1"],           // One or more sets of timers
          "time": 1.0,                // Time in seconds to skip (float) 
          "trigger": {                                         
            // ...                    // Normal triggers used
          }
        }
      ],
      "alerts": [                     // works for alerts, sounds, marker, directions
        {
           // ...
           "set": "set1"              // TimerSet you wanna use in actions, won't harm if set is not used or, auto predefined to "default"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

